<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tinos</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tinos is an island of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyclades">Cyclades</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aegean">Aegean Sea</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>. Taken around 1207 by the Venetian Ghisi family and ruled directly by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> from 1390, it held out longer than any other Venetian possession in the Aegean, until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> took it in 1715. Its Church of Panagia Evangelistria is the most important <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-orthodox-church">Orthodox</a> pilgrimage shrine in Greece.</p></div>
